kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "yaml-dsl-demand-imports-scope"
purpose: "定义 demand imports (`imports` / `$import`) 的作用域边界，确保其仅服务于稳定的 authoring 复用场景，而非 runtime overlay 或 output extras 的替代机制。 [scope-review-2026-07-12-c20]"
valid_scope[1]: src/scalim/
requirements[4]{req_id,title,statement}:
  r1,demand imports MUST remain available for reusable authoring fragments,"demand `imports` / `$import` MUST 继续服务于跨文件 authoring 复用: - imports MUST 继续支持 demand 侧片段共享 - 允许范围 MUST 绑定到稳定 authoring surface,而不是 runtime overlay / control-plane"
  r2,demand imports scope MUST be limited to stable authoring surfaces,"`$import` 的允许范围 MUST 限制在 demand 的稳定 authoring surfaces: - `main_source` - `sources.*` - `fields.*` - `relations.*` - `resources.*` 中仍属于资源声明的部分"
  r3,workflow MUST NOT support imports expansion,"workflow MUST NOT 支持 imports expansion: - workflow schema MUST 不暴露 `$import` 作为受支持结构 - workflow validate / compile MUST 不接受 workflow fragment imports 作为主线路径"
  r4,imports MUST NOT become a substitute for runtime overlay or output extras,"imports MUST 仅解决“跨文件共享 authoring 片段”的问题,而不是替代 runtime overlay、profile 或 output extras: - imports MUST NOT 用于重建 runtime policy 配置面 - imports MUST NOT 用于恢复已迁出的 output extras authoring surface"
scenarios[8]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  r1,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r1,"demand-reuses-a-resource-declaration-fragment-from-another-f",某个 demand YAML 通过 `imports` 引入外部片段文件,用户在稳定 authoring surface 中使用 `$import` 引用该片段,系统 MUST 成功展开该 authoring 片段
  r2,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r2,"runtime-policy-paths-are-not-importable","",用户尝试在 runtime policy 或 output extras 等非稳定 authoring surface 中使用 `$import`,系统 MUST 拒绝该写法
  r3,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r3,"workflow-import-syntax-is-rejected",某个 workflow YAML 试图声明 `imports` 或 `$import`,系统对该 workflow 进行 schema 校验或编译,系统 MUST 拒绝该结构
  r4,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r4,"imports-is-evaluated-by-reuse-value-rather-than-overlay-conv","",某个新字段希望接入 imports 机制,审核标准 MUST 先判断它是否属于稳定 authoring surface